Verifier hooks: per-transaction cryptographic checks by components outside the rules engine.

rules.py (run_hooks) calls each executable fullnode/hooks/<name> once per window:

    hooks/<name> <list file>

Each line of the list file is a base path P (work/rules/hooks/<name>/<height>_<txidx>) with:
  P.tx    the raw transaction bytes (sliced from the block by the sizes blockdelta printed)
  P.ctx   the spent transparent outputs, in follow's txx ctx layout:
          u32 len | len bytes of amounts (i64 LE each, in input order) |
          u32 len | len bytes of scriptPubKeys (CompactSize-prefixed, in input order)
          (both lengths 0 when the tx has no transparent inputs; coinbase: no inputs)
  P.json  {"height", "txidx", "txid" (display order), "version", "branch_id" (8 hex, v5/v6; 0 before)}

The hook prints exactly one line per item:

    verdict <height> <txidx> PASS
    verdict <height> <txidx> FAIL <reason>

Any FAIL, or an item without a verdict line, rejects the window (nothing is committed).
If hooks/<name> does not exist (or is not executable), rules.py reports
"<name>: SKIPPED (component pending) for N tx" and records it in the window's meta
(rules.hooks) — it is never counted as a pass.

Which transactions go to which hook (rules.hook_jobs):
  transparent  every tx with transparent inputs: scripts, ECDSA, ZIP 243/244 sighash
               (component: transparent/)                              -> PENDING (absent)
  sapling      every tx with Sapling spends/outputs or Sprout JoinSplits: Groth16 / BCTV14
               proofs, spend-auth and binding sigs, joinSplitSig
               (components: sapling/, sapling/groth16/)               -> PENDING (absent)
  orchard      every tx with an Orchard or Ironwood bundle (coinbase included): RedPallas
               spend-auth + binding sigs and Halo 2 proofs, via follow/bin/txx and
               follow/bin/halo2_batch (+ halo2_one to pinpoint)       -> PRESENT (hooks/orchard)

Note: hooks/orchard verifies with the post-NU6.3 circuit build follow uses; it is meant for
blocks above the last checkpoint (3,522,460, NU6.3 era). Earlier Orchard circuit versions are
not routed here (blocks below the checkpoint are checkpointed, not proof-verified).
